.TH BOX-MIGRATE 1 "November 2026" "Box-Migrate 0.9.5" "User Commands"

.\" ============================================================================
.SH NAME
.\" ============================================================================

box-migrate \- upgrade and migrate packages, repositories, and caches between Toolbox containers

.\" ============================================================================
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" ============================================================================

.B box-migrate
.I SOURCE DESTINATION
.RI [ OPTIONS ]

.\" ============================================================================
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" ============================================================================

.B box-migrate
creates a new Toolbox container at a newer release and populates it with 
the packages from an existing container, saving you from reinstalling everything by hand.
.PP
Particularly useful on immutable systems like Fedora Silverblue, 
.B box-migrate
reads the packages explicitly installed in your source container, checks what is already 
present in the new destination container, and installs the remaining packages.
.PP
Repositories, GPG keys, and local caches can also be transferred. The source container remains 
unmodified during standard operations (though optional local RPM reconstruction via 
\fB--rebuild-local\fP may install \fBrpmrebuild\fP into it if missing), and the destination 
is created as an isolated container.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH OPTIONS
.\" ============================================================================

.SS Destination Setup

.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-distro " " DISTRO
The distribution for your new destination container.
This option is required (unless a custom image is provided via \fB--image\fP).
.IP
Supported default distributions include:
.BR fedora ,
.BR rhel ,
.BR ubuntu ,
and
.BR arch .
If an unsupported distribution is specified in an interactive terminal, 
you will be prompted to supply a custom container image reference.

.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-release " " RELEASE
The release version or codename for the destination container
(such as \fI45\fP for Fedora or \fInoble\fP for Ubuntu).
Required for versioned distributions; omitted or ignored for rolling-release distributions like Arch.
Automatically ignored or overridden if a custom container image is specified.

.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-image " " IMAGE
Specify a custom container image reference (such as \fIquay.io/rockylinux/rockylinux:9\fP) 
when using a distribution that is not natively supported or when overriding defaults.
Triggers an immediate pre-flight container inspection to validate package manager 
compatibility before any layers are pulled or allocated.

.SS Migration Behavior

.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Preview the migration safely.
.B box-migrate
will inspect the source and export data, but it will not create the destination 
container or install any packages.

.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-repos
Migrate custom repositories and GPG keys, updating version numbers so they match 
your new release.
This is enabled by default.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-repos
Disable repository and GPG key migration.

.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-cache
Migrate local package caches to help with offline or manual package installation.
This is enabled by default.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Disable package cache migration.

.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-rebuild\-local
Rebuild and migrate standalone local RPM packages (one-off files installed without 
an associated repository) using
.BR rpmrebuild (1)
via
.BR sudo (8).
.IP
This applies only to DNF-based distributions and is disabled by default.

.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workdir " " DIR
Specify a custom directory to store logs, manifests, and archives.
.IP
By default, files are saved to
.IR ~/box-migrate-SOURCE-to-DESTINATION/ .

.SS General

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH SUPPORTED DISTRIBUTIONS
.\" ============================================================================

.B box-migrate
migrates containers within the same package manager family (APT, DNF, or Pacman). 
Cross-family migrations are automatically caught and aborted during pre-flight checks.
.PP
Container ancestry (\fBID\fR and \fBID_LIKE\fP fields in \fI/etc/os-release\fP) is used 
to support derivative distributions automatically.

.TP
.B DNF (RPM-based)
Natively supports
.B fedora
and
.B rhel
as default distributions, alongside DNF-based custom images (such as Rocky Linux or AlmaLinux).

.TP
.B APT (Debian-based)
Natively supports
.B ubuntu
and
.B debian
as default/custom targets, alongside APT-compatible derivatives.

.TP
.B Pacman (Arch-based)
Natively supports
.B arch
and compatible Arch derivatives.

.\" ============================================================================
.SH EXAMPLES
.\" ============================================================================

.TP
.B Upgrade a standard Fedora container
.nf
box-migrate fedora-toolbox-44 fedora-toolbox-45 -d fedora -r 45
.fi

.TP
.B Migrate an Arch container (rolling release, no release flag needed)
.nf
box-migrate arch-source arch-dest -d arch
.fi

.TP
.B Migrate using a custom container image
.nf
box-migrate deb-source rocky-dest -i quay.io/rockylinux/rockylinux:9 -L
.fi

.TP
.B Preview a migration safely
.nf
box-migrate fedora-toolbox-44 fedora-toolbox-45 -d fedora -r 45 --dry-run
.fi

.\" ============================================================================
.SH SEE ALSO
.\" ============================================================================

.BR toolbox (1),
.BR podman (1),
.BR dnf (8),
.BR apt (8),
.BR pacman (8)